# The oracle fixtures are pinned by hash: inst/extdata/oracle-manifest.yml
# records an MD5 and a SHA-256 for each, and tests/testthat/test-oracle-manifest.R
# checks the shipped bytes against them on every run.
#
# Git's end-of-line translation would defeat that. On a Windows checkout the
# default conversion rewrites LF to CRLF, changing every fixture's bytes and so
# its hash, while leaving the numbers read from them identical -- the values
# parse the same, so the oracle grade still passes and only the identity check
# fails. That is the right outcome from the gate and the wrong state for the
# repository: a hash-pinned fixture must be byte-identical on every platform,
# or the hash records a property of the checkout rather than of the fixture.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion, so these files are delivered verbatim
# everywhere. Found by the fixture gate failing on windows-latest, 2026-07-15.
oracle/*.csv                -text
aciR/inst/extdata/*.csv     -text

# The MATLAB harnesses are the provenance of those fixtures; keep them stable
# too, so a hash taken of a harness means the same thing on any platform.
oracle/*.m                  -text
